 @ResolveReviews  But the default RGB stripe layout from other panels such as IPS has its own fringing, right? That's what ClearType exists to solve in the first place.

If what you're saying means that those QD-OLED displays have significantly increased fringing that affects even content that isn't as fine-detail as text, then I get how ClearType itself couldn't solve that. In that case I've been kind of getting the wrong idea of the situation because I've only ever heard these fringing issues described when it comes to text, though.

I'm curious now if that's the actual problem, in which case this all would be highly dependent on the exact details of pixel layouts such as gaps inbetween pixels etc, rather than a more simple pixel ordering/alignment issue as you can for example use BGR displays just fine with changing ClearType settings (because of them supporting that layout, and it only visibly affecting text quality, of course) as I did with my previous monitor.

