 @ysesh463  No absolutely not  banding has nothing to do with the white subpixel in W-OLED.  TFT Central has an excellent article ( Exploring the “Grey Banding” Issue Affecting Some Tandem WOLED Panels ) and provides an accurate explanation : 

Quote :  '' This phenomenon originates from the inherent physical characteristics of the Tandem OLED driving layer (DDI) when operating at extremely low luminance levels. Under near-black brightness conditions, the DAC (Digital-to-Analog Converter) outputs extremely small driving currents. Measurements show a fixed, minor micro-current variation between different driving channels '' 

There can be as much as 30% variation in the value of the current those channels receive when the screen is in near black conditions  which is what creates the banding since not all regions of the screen receive the same current and thus are not lit uniformly .

